The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
} else if (new_view->type == C_ROOT || new_view->type == C_OUTPUT) {
```
Reason:
This condition incorrectly checks for both `C_ROOT` and `C_OUTPUT` types, leading to the function returning false when an output is provided instead of setting the focus to the associated workspace. This prevents users from switching focus effectively between outputs.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
} else if (new_view->type == C_ROOT) {
    sway_log(L_DEBUG, "Not setting focus above the workspace level");
    return false;
} else if (new_view->type == C_OUTPUT) {
    return set_focused_container(swayc_active_workspace_for(new_view));
```
Reason:
The patch separates the handling of `C_ROOT` and `C_OUTPUT`. It allows the function to correctly set the focus to the workspace associated with the output when `C_OUTPUT` is encountered, thus enabling users to switch focus between outputs effectively.

